#edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560940 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560940 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560940 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186560428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560940 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "af354a29-8f42-5155-a64c-ca4506ba75c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560953 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560953 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560953 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560953 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560953 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560953 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560953 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560953 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186560385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560953 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d125b15d-4f81-5935-b076-db66967f564d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560959 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560959 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560959 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560959 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186560597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560959 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "de285235-a8d6-5932-a9ac-01bfdef66d64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560974 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560974 #edb/ref 1069 "q-45061" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560974 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560974 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of the sequence\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)+5,\\,\\,f(1)=4,\\,\\,n\\ge 1?\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560974 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d53c105-6357-5aa5-b9db-2ac9c9ee796f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560974 #edb/ref 1074 "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term $f(1)$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is $f(1)=4,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =f(1)+5 \\\\  & =4+5 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =f(2)-f(1) \\\\  & =9-4 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $f(1)=4$ and $d=5$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =4+(n-1)(5) \\\\  & =4+5n-5 \\\\  & =5n-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\nf(n)=5n-1,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560975 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560975 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560975 #edb/ref 1069 "q-236696" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560975 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560975 #edb/ref 1071 "The formula for the $n$th term of a sequence is $f(n)=1-6n$ for $n\\ge 1.$ The recursive formula for this sequence is\n\n$f(n+1)=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,f(1)=$\n{{field-2}},\n$\\,n\\ge 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560975 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d952218-06b1-5f09-827d-2a6a5b13b0f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560975 #edb/ref 1074 "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence is as follows:\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)+d,\\,f(1)=___\\,,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =1-6(1)=-5 \\\\ f(2) & =1-6(2)=-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =f(2)-f(1) \\\\  & =-11-(-5) \\\\  & =-11+5 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is $f(1)=-5$ and the common difference is $d=-6.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)-6,\\,f(1)=-5,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560987 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560987 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560987 #edb/ref 1069 "q-236692" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560987 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560987 #edb/ref 1071 "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is ${a}_{n}=1-9n$ for $n\\ge 1.$ The recursive formula for this sequence is\n\n${a}_{n+1}=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,{a}_{1}=$\n{{field-2}},\n$\\,n\\ge 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560987 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2e740a26-9734-5997-8349-4d773f862d1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560987 #edb/ref 1074 "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence is as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+d,\\,{a}_{1}=___\\,,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =1-9(1)=-8 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =1-9(2)=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =-17-(-8) \\\\  & =-17+8 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is ${a}_{1}=-8$ and the common difference is $d=-9.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-9,\\,{a}_{1}=-8,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560995 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560995 #edb/ref 1069 "q-45058" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560995 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560995 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of the arithmetic sequence\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-3,\\,\\,{a}_{1}=7,\\,\\,n\\ge 1?\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560995 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "424dd539-6c70-5877-8bbc-fc51ba75e083" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560995 #edb/ref 1074 "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is ${a}_{1}=7,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}-3 \\\\  & =7-3 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =4-7 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute ${a}_{1}=7$ and $d=-3$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =7+(n-1)(-3) \\\\  & =7-3n+3 \\\\  & =-3n+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=-3n+10,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561005 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560882 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561005 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108596" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561005 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561005 #edb/ref 1071 "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is $f(n)=5n-4$ for $n\\ge 1.$  What is the recursive formula for this sequence?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561005 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6500f3df-ea0f-5675-b52f-b066bf2e3cba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561005 #edb/ref 1074 "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is as follows:\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)+d,\\,f(1)=___\\,,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =5(1)-4=1 \\\\ f(2) & =5(2)-4=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =f(2)-f(1) \\\\  & =6-1 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is $f(1)=1$ and the common difference is $d=5.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)+5,\\,f(1)=1,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561011 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561011 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108594" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561011 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561011 #edb/ref 1071 "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is ${a}_{n}=5n+8$ for $n\\ge 1.$  What is the recursive formula for this sequence?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561011 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6cfbc389-30d9-53d7-b8c8-e6f86312705b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561011 #edb/ref 1074 "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence is as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+d,\\,{a}_{1}=___\\,,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =5(1)+8=13 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =5(2)+8=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =18-13 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is ${a}_{1}=13$ and the common difference is $d=5.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+5,\\,{a}_{1}=13,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561033 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561033 #edb/ref 1069 "q-236728" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561033 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561033 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following arithmetic sequence:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-8,\\,\\,{a}_{1}=2,\\,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nThe explicit formula for the $n$th term is\n\n${a}_{n}=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,n\\ge 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561033 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9e6b4405-b1f3-59b3-b412-8d0c0e5d7557" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561033 #edb/ref 1074 "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is ${a}_{1}=2,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}-8 \\\\  & =2-8 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =-6-2 \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute ${a}_{1}=2$ and $d=-8$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =2+(n-1)(-8) \\\\  & =2-8n+8 \\\\  & =10-8n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=10-8n,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561053 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561053 #edb/ref 1069 "q-45060" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561053 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561053 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of the sequence\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)-7,\\,\\,f(1)=-1,\\,\\,n\\ge 1?\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561053 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df1d75ef-4d29-5e1f-bd95-e67ad6f7bd69" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561053 #edb/ref 1074 "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term $f(1)$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is $f(1)=-1,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =f(1)-7 \\\\  & =-1-7 \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =f(2)-f(1) \\\\  & =-8-(-1) \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $f(1)=-1$ and $d=-7$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-1+(n-1)(-7) \\\\  & =-1-7n+7 \\\\  & =-7n+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\nf(n)=-7n+6,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
